<h2>Lighting in Texas's first Dark Sky Community</h2>
<p>Dripping Springs was the first city in Texas designated an International Dark Sky Community, and the night sky is part of why people move here. That shapes everything about landscape lighting Dripping Springs TX homeowners should expect. The city's outdoor lighting ordinance requires fully shielded fixtures, favors warm color temperatures and limits how much light a property can put out, and most HOAs in Belterra, Headwaters, Caliterra and the surrounding communities echo those rules. Austin Landscape Lighting welcomes this. Low-voltage LED landscape lighting done well is exactly what dark-sky guidelines ask for: small amounts of warm light placed precisely on stone, trees, steps and entries, with nothing aimed at the sky and nothing visible from the road but a softly lit home.</p>
